jitIfNoValueT -- SEQ 384 R1 (Tony, 2026-10-19): an IF whose condition has no value runs once per fire.
The condition is a COMMAND call (dumpContents), which emits no value, so the whole IF is handed to run time
(jitIfRT). But the condition was already EVALUATED at build to find that out -- so the dump prints once at build
and once per fire. Count the ivDump lines in each segment: today 2 then 1 (the build's plus fire 1's, then fire 2's);
intended 1 then 1, = the interpreted twin. ivN reads 1 then 2 either way.
